CSharpier — https://github.com/belav/csharpier
Licensed under the MIT License.

Kerf is an independent implementation, not a fork: no CSharpier source is copied
into this repository. However, several algorithms and models in Kerf are
recognisably derived from CSharpier's approach, and that debt is acknowledged here:

  - The document-layout algorithm (group break propagation, the flat/break fits
    measurement, and the conditional-group construct).
  - The syntax-trivia model: how leading and trailing trivia, comments, blank-line
    collapsing, preprocessor directives, disabled `#if` text and regions are
    attached to tokens and printed.
  - The golden-file testing convention in which a fixture with no companion
    expectation file must format to itself.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Prettier — https://github.com/prettier/prettier
Licensed under the MIT License.

The underlying document intermediate representation (concat/group/line/indent/
if-break) originates with Prettier, which in turn builds on Philip Wadler's
"A prettier printer" (1997) and Derek Oppen's "Prettyprinting" (1980).

